# Build artifacts -- unanchored, so nested crates under experiments/ match too
target/
# ...but `target/` matches only that exact name, and concurrent milestones each
# need their own CARGO_TARGET_DIR to avoid lock contention, so they invent
# names like `target-m77/` and `.cargo-target-orch/`. Four such directories
# were carrying 2.5 GB while matching none of the rules above. Same lesson as
# the *.npy rule below: ignore by SHAPE, not by the locations someone
# remembered.
target-*/
.cargo-target*/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Stacked output and test renders -- never commit heavy binaries
/out/
*.tif
*.tiff
*.dng
*.exr
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# RAW inputs are never committed
*.ARW
*.arw
*.NEF
*.CR2
*.CR3
*.RAF
*.ORF
*.RW2

# Local benchmark and profiling output
*.json.gz
/bench-results/
/profiles/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
experiments/*/out/cache/
experiments/m30-hdr-cobracket/out/cache/

# Regenerable numeric artifacts, ignored by FORMAT not location.
# A 455 MB focus volume reached a commit and was rejected by GitHub's 100 MB
# limit because it sat in experiments/m31-verification/out/ rather than in
# experiments/*/out/cache/, which was the only ignored path. Location-based
# rules only cover the directories someone remembered; these formats are
# always regenerable, so ignore them everywhere.
*.npy
*.npz
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# ...except these two, which are committed RESULTS rather than caches and are
# already tracked (gitignore does not untrack, but state the intent).
!experiments/m29-static-defects/out/static-109.npy
!experiments/m39-verify/out/07-merged-rois.npz
